From e388c90c7172d2ddefabf4cdcfd57adf7d83c666 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:25:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/28] (b) v2: caption hooks, typeset socket, float target,
 subfloat/box

Revision of the caption interface of (b), on top of it:

- \caption reads the star and the arguments itself (no \@dblarg; an
  absent optional argument is \NoValue) and executes the new hook
  caption/before {type}{star}{opt}{text} before the step.
- \@caption keeps its signature; it executes the new hook
  caption/prepare {type}{star}{list text}{text}, the socket
  caption/listentry (now 3 arguments: type, list text, text) and the new
  socket caption/typeset {type}{star}{text}, whose kernel plug
  \@kernel@caption@typeset does the old grouping and \@makecaption.
- Switches \if@captionstep and \if@captiontarget, honoured by the kernel
  plug \@kernel@caption@step of caption/step (no \stepcounter
  redefinition); reset with \if@captionstar at the end of \@caption.
- The step uses the float target \@floatHref@<type> if it is set.
- Kernel copies \@kernel@caption and \@kernel@@caption, undefined after
  a latexrelease roll-back (the availability test for clients).
- lttagging: tagging socket subfloat/box.
- latex-lab-float: no plug for caption/step any more; \@floatHref@<type>
  set at the float start and in float/split (captions after float/split
  used a target that is never made); generic structure names also for an
  undefined \@captype; subfloat/box plugs: the next minipage or \parbox
  becomes the Part of the sub-float instead of a Div; plugs nolabel for
  the label tagging sockets of \caption* (wide \caption* captions gave
  unbalanced para hooks).
- Tests: caption-interface-001 rewritten, caption-interface-002 (roll-back),
  float-020 updated (subfloat/box), float-023 (float targets); float-004:
  the caption after float/split now uses floatstructure.N; .tlg updates
  for the new release block and the two hooks.
- float-025/026 (from (c)): the class \@makecaption now gets the label
  \csname fnum@figure\endcsname, as the kernel \@caption expands the type.
